commit b7f49b8c4155338ab2b58b40120893aa70052472
Author: haileen5 <haileen5@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 23 11:18:51 2026 +0000

    fix(#1220): use daisyUI neutral pair for the active sidebar item
    
    daisyUI paints [aria-current=page] with --menu-active-fg (--color-neutral-content), while MaryUI paints the background with bg-base-300. The two token families collide in light (1.09:1), cupcake and fantasy (1.01:1); fantasy is the default theme.
    
    Owner decision (issue #1220) is option C: keep the pair inside daisyUI's own neutral family. Passing active-bg-color="bg-neutral text-neutral-content" to x-menu does that in all seven themes and also cascades to the open submenu header (the gate accepts either header pair; both stay readable). aria-current, mary-active-menu, MaryUI itself, the glass block and inactive hover are untouched.
    
    Measured active contrast: light 15.71, dark 15.71, synthwave 5.58, coffee 11.54, cupcake 11.90, fantasy 9.46, luxury 13.54. The new e2e spec pins the computed pair and the >=4.5 ratio for every theme.

